  "notes": [
   "The QB, WR and TE grids all rank opponents on the same pass-defense metric, EPA allowed per eligible pass play, so they rank opponents identically: they are not separate per-position models. RB uses EPA allowed per designed rush. Each defense is ranked among defenses with at least 3 presumed-complete games before the week (rank 1 = most permissive).",
   "A player's row uses his current NFL team for every remaining week. The grid describes the opponent defenses only: it says nothing about the player's role, usage or health, and future trades, releases and signings are not predicted.",
   "A defense's allowed numbers describe what offenses did against it; they also reflect the offenses it faced and game situations, and say nothing about an individual player's role or usage.",
   "No lookahead: each week uses only the opponent's games presumed complete before that week; future weeks use every game presumed complete so far."
  ],
